# Sane defaults for everything else.
* text=auto

# A .vl is a vvvv gamma document, and a corrupted one fails SILENTLY - vvvv simply does not load
# it, with no error anywhere. So its bytes are pinned rather than left to whatever core.autocrlf a
# contributor happens to have.
#
# Verified rather than assumed: git stores and returns the UTF-8 BOM verbatim (the sibling
# repository's committed VL.Mapsui.vl blob begins EF BB BF), and this machine has
# core.autocrlf=false. Neither of those is true of every clone, which is the point of this line.
#
# "text eol=crlf" rather than "-text": it keeps .vl diffable, which matters because the rule in
# this repository is that the checked-in .vl is the source of truth and is edited in place, with
# every edit validated. A readable diff is part of that validation.
*.vl text eol=crlf

# Same reasoning, same silent failure: Help.xml orders the help patches and carries their search
# tags, and vvvv ignores a malformed one without complaint.
Help.xml text eol=crlf
